    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d804">

                <pb facs="1147" n="1127" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795A.00/11–1050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Mission at
                        the United Nations</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-10-10T19:00:00-05:00">November 10,
                            1950—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>495. Dept thinks it wld be useful if when reps of IC have established themselves
                    and are available to lend assistance on questions relating to NK frontier in
                    accordance with IC res of Nov 6[<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>],<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d804-f1"/> they shld report this fact to SYG. SYG in turn might then
                    arrange to make authorities in Peiping aware of availability of IC’s reps.</p>
                <p>Suggest you talk to SYG and perhaps Romulo along these lines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d804-f1" n="1" xml:id="d804-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram 303, November 9, noon, to Seoul, <ref target="#pg1115">p.
                    1115</ref>.</p>
            </note>
